  The reel_script says the caller claimed there was a bomb ('பாம் இருப்பதாக') at Gandhipuram bus stand as the opening fact, but the article only says he mistakenly said 'பாம் கால்' instead of 'ஸ்பேம் கால்'; he did not claim a bomb was present, so this is an inaccurate framing.
  The reel_script states the 45-year-old 'புதிய மொபைல் எண் வாங்கினார்' and then 'தொடர்ந்து அழைப்புகள் வந்ததால்' — the article says he called to report continuous calls, which is consistent, but the reel_script omits the article's explicit point that the caller was mistaken, which is partially covered; however the reel_script's 'பதற்றத்தில்' detail is present, so this is fine.
  The reel_script's 'சோதனை நடத்தினர்' describes the search as a full bus-stand search, consistent with the article, but the headline and slides present the search as caused by 'பாம் கால்' as if an actual bomb threat existed, which conflicts with the article's conclusion that the call was a mistaken spam-call remark.
  The caption's headline line '‘ஸ்பேம் கால்’ என்பதற்குப் பதில் ‘பாம் கால்’ எனக் கூறியதால் காந்திபுரத்தில் போலீஸ் சோதனை' is grammatically ambiguous and frames the mistake as the cause of the search in a way that obscures the actual sequence, though the body text is accurate.
  The slides_spec hl1 'தவறுதலாக ‘பாம் கால்’; காந்திபுரத்தில்' and hl2 'ஸ்பேம் கால்கள் மட்டுமே' are fragmentary and unclear in Tamil meaning, mixing two facts awkwardly in a headline.
